Good point. I was thinking about this a bit more, and I think maybe
the better choice is to leave Snickersnee more or less as-is, but
perhaps with a slight increase in damage (+1d12, say, instead of +1d8,
so there's a reason to wield it instead of Excalibur), then to add in
Kusanagi as a short sword which is a Sam's first sac gift (but would
be wishable, non-intelligent, able to be randomly generated, etc).
Then, replace the Tsurugi with the Katana of Masamune which offers
similar properties (+d8 damage, bisection, acts as a luckstone). Then,
make it so Kusanagi (but not Snickersnee) will submit to being wielded
alongside the Katana of Masamune. This would make the Katana, which
would otherwise be only somewhat better than Vorpal Blade and not as
good as Excalibur or Grayswandir, a viable choice for Samurai. (Unlike
the Tsurugi, which is a pretty dubious choice).


So:

Snickersnee, lawful katana: +1d5 to-hit, +1d12 damage versus all.

Kusanagi, lawful short sword: +1d4 to-hit, +1d8 damage versus all,
submits to being wielded in the offhand alongside the Katana of
Masamune ONLY by Samurai.

Katana of Masamune, lawful Samurai katana: +1d8 damage versus all, 5%
chance to bisect (as Tsurugi), acts as a luckstone when carried,
confers stealth when wielded.



